Both worktrees reviewed read-only (no edits). Suite + `node --check` run in each.

## Worktree: `chopshop-studio-dnd` (`feature/drag-drop`)

**Verdict:** FIX-FIRST

**Suite:**
- `bin/rails test` → `401 runs, 4161 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skips` (baseline 395 + 6 new; green)
- `node --check app/javascript/aether.js` → OK

**Findings:**
1. **BLOCKING** — `app/views/jobs/show.html.erb:256`: `proof_drag = %( ... data-scrap-name="#{proof_png}").html_safe` interpolates the runner-supplied proof filename into a raw HTML attribute with `.html_safe`, bypassing ERB escaping. A `"` or ` onmouseover=…` in `v.manifest["proof"]` breaks out of the attribute — the HTML-injection path the brief warns about. (The source/inverse/candidate attrs use auto-escaped `<%= %>`; only this one is raw.)
2. **BLOCKING (functional)** — `app/views/composites/show.html.erb:114` + `:172`: the brief requires dragging a thumbnail *from the picker* onto `#compCanvas`, but `#compScrapPicker` is a `.popup` (`position:fixed; inset:0; z-index:9600`, CSS:3433) with an opaque backdrop over the canvas. `dragover`/`drop` land on the overlay, never on the canvas, so the picker drag path does nothing. The drawer path works.
3. **NIT** — `app/views/composites/show.html.erb:181`: the canvas drop handler falls back to any `text/plain` payload as the layer URL (`getData('text/plain')`) with no allow-list, so an arbitrary dragged string/URL becomes a layer. Parsed-but-unvalidated payload.
4. **NIT** — `app/javascript/aether.js:1029`: `scrapDrag.item` is assigned but never read (only `scrapDrag.fav` is consumed); dead state.

**Hard-rule violations:** none (no hostnames/IPs/paths, no new deps, no credential touched, still uncommitted). Note: `dragleave` child-guard at `aether.js:1060-1065` is correct (`relatedTarget && target.contains(...)` → keep; null/outside → clear).

## Worktree: `chopshop-studio-preview` (`feature/preview-popups`)

**Verdict:** SHIP

**Suite:**
- `bin/rails test` → `405 runs, 4194 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skips` (baseline 395 + 10 new; green)
- `node --check app/javascript/aether.js` → OK

**Findings (all NIT, none blocking):**
1. **NIT** — `app/javascript/aether.js:840` reads `token.content` while `csReusePreview` at `:770` (and `csUseAsSource`) uses `token.getAttribute('content')`. Both resolve to `HTMLMetaElement.content`, so this is a style inconsistency, not a defect.
2. **NIT** — `app/controllers/jobs_controller.rb:177-200`: `#reuse` checks only runner `status==200 && body.present?`, unlike `use_inverse` (`:148`) which also verifies the PNG magic bytes. A runner 200 with non-PNG bytes would be stored as an upload.
3. **NIT** — `app/javascript/aether.js:782-790`: `csLoadForCanvas` resolves immediately only when `naturalWidth || width` is truthy; on an already-broken image (`complete === true`, `naturalWidth === 0`, error already fired) no listener ever fires, so Save silently does nothing.

Verified against the brief: `#reuse` accepts only `source.png`/`source.inverse.png` and never auto-runs (spec cloned to `session[:spec_draft]`); toolbox binds only when `.cs-modal-art img`/`#csViewerImg` exists (non-image popups untouched); hue is a CSS `filter` on the `<img>` (no file mutation); Save canvas-exports main+reference with `ctx.filter` baked and POSTs `/scrapbook/import`. `[hidden]` is complete — a global `[hidden]{display:none!important}` (CSS:326) already covers the toolbar controls and `.cs-ref-img`.

**Hard-rule violations:** none (no hostnames/IPs/paths, no new deps, no credential touched, composite/import validation untouched, still uncommitted).
